## Known problems

Measured weaknesses and cases the runs could not reach, each with what was
observed.
{{with .M8}}
- **Pending budget spend dies with its replica.** Costs a replica settles
  on grace are kept in its memory until Redis answers again. In M8 the
  replica killed during an outage took {{.LostBefore}} with it before the grace
  fix and {{.LostAfter}} after it (its allowance was already spent). The loss is
  at most one allowance ({{.Grace}}) plus the requests it had reserved on Redis
  before the outage and settled during it; a replica killed late in its
  first outage would come close.
- **A settle that timed out after Redis applied it is charged twice.**
  The replica cannot tell it from one that never arrived, so it keeps the
  cost as pending and charges it again: an over-count, never a miss. Not
  observed in M8: no reconciliation gap was negative in either run.
- **A hold whose replica died while Redis was up expires without its cost
  reaching `spent`.** The request was sent upstream; nobody settles it,
  and after the reservation TTL the hold is released. Not reached by M8,
  whose kill came during an outage (`reserved` was 0 at every snapshot);
  Q6's replica kill, with Redis up, is the case, and its reconciliation is
  not recorded.
{{else}}
- Budget reconciliation under a flapping store: not measured yet
  (`make chaos-flap`).
{{end}}- **About two seconds degraded after Redis comes back.** go-redis's
  dial backoff and the gateway's one-second probe run one after the
  other, so a replica keeps using its local limits, grace and no cache for
  about two seconds after Redis is ready (M9, every mode). The cache is
  the visible cost: hits lost, not wrong answers.
- **`everysec` can lose the last second of charges.** A Redis crash in
  the middle of a key's spending forgets up to a second of its writes;
  M9's crash came after the budget had run out, so it lost none. With no
  append-only file (`REDIS_PERSIST=none`, Q6) a restart forgets every
  budget.
- **A `LOADING` Redis was not reached under load.** M9's append-only file
  loaded in tens of milliseconds and no replica called during it; the integration
  test shows a `LOADING` reply degrades like an unreachable store and
  recovers, but no chaos run has a Redis that loads for seconds.

